{"title":"2015 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Solve in integers the equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a563dd59e15d5c2022ae9f69c6be35c042bec806.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2+xy+y^2 = \\left(\\frac{x+y}{3}+1\\right)^3.\\]\" width=\"240\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/21363140fbe1a1f51c21f6c4731f1d56dd9a650d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APBQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" /> is inscribed in circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/8/ac80bc77394a33c3e18143e17c43d1b261ab1ae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle P = \\angle Q = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/b/86baca28012c300e13ead6015a3b9f2bd8a75953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = AQ &lt; BP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"133\" height=\"16\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be a variable point on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0deaae00f6af4ac1f5882568e7b6667bb334a2ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{PQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"19\" />. Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d857b2c804701b561a5c8c90c400f360d27232c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"13\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> (other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />). Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> lies on arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/c/26cc35adb36da24d8436f0d49b7cdb3065061d43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/e/c3e8571374bd200b0a9b5331e9501145c838c806.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{XT}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba52c969bed0d101e945b960e9e2b96604fcadb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AX}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> denote the midpoint of chord <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27c79d1720945ed79ebd44d6bf48bba9ba3e5bca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{ST}$\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> varies on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0deaae00f6af4ac1f5882568e7b6667bb334a2ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{PQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"19\" />, show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> moves along a circle.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/c/2ccc48ee56a4a21a8cd7b2cb70eaacd4ef46fa3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\{1, 2, ..., n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897470a282b6b85fa5221eacd41369b9a157f491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. Each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> subsets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is to be colored red or blue. (The subset itself is assigned a color and not its individual elements.) For any set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/6/20641e11b1c854b428d63554c50c258f43c15812.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T \\subseteq S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />, we then write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/9587f4255ca590d37018e5703bef62e537354e41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(T)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> for the number of subsets of T that are blue.\n</p><p>Determine the number of colorings that satisfy the following condition: for any subsets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c073f8a05257a19c2dacc368858763bb44fa3747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/d/40db9b6f10ff583906d78a06a76e08e04381bc1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/5/1e5371f0639b2a8ed04d6b74c7401b1d36264652.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(T_1)f(T_2) = f(T_1 \\cup T_2)f(T_1 \\cap T_2).\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Steve is piling <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed99c85dd00eb11d60bb8d0332530445cf25c5ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> indistinguishable stones on the squares of an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f761f7fc79f2bec21a2f31c896840d6f36cdc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\times n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> grid. Each square can have an arbitrarily high pile of stones. After he finished piling his stones in some manner, he can then perform stone moves, defined as follows. Consider any four grid squares, which are corners of a rectangle, i.e. in positions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0b533f1c1f3a68bacf9f4856b83f67898aaa73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, k), (i, l), (j, k), (j, l)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72d3d6c286899a6607c08c5c500816d1bf70f345.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq i, j, k, l\\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c8b76bca5358138116d4d962e20e582bfa708b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i&lt;j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20ccf57f7714b83f64a8ef7e1bd9e18ccfbe78d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;l$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />. A stone move consists of either removing one stone from each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/c/6ec83d11312e52717655024b28bbde1050b97198.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e579d3552c24aaaccbc4559c92f9291e6e69d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(j, l)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> and moving them to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ea35c25b8931e32f87157fd76853f9200902acc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, l)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472226e072e2a15cf4e76b655a5b11bd1bce21f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(j, k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> respectively, or removing one stone from each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ea35c25b8931e32f87157fd76853f9200902acc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, l)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472226e072e2a15cf4e76b655a5b11bd1bce21f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(j, k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and moving them to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/c/6ec83d11312e52717655024b28bbde1050b97198.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e579d3552c24aaaccbc4559c92f9291e6e69d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(j, l)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>Two ways of piling the stones are equivalent if they can be obtained from one another by a sequence of stone moves.\n</p><p>How many different non-equivalent ways can Steve pile the stones on the grid?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00cbe98d2864aae78c25b55b49ae5482c8a50e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c, d, e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> be distinct positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e201f0e5daa93bcf054a1706b50ea281abd5885.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^4 + b^4 = c^4 + d^4 = e^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"172\" height=\"16\" />. Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/8/138b1aaec3d513b54bfe700836ef8ffe6784344e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ac + bd$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> is a composite number.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/e/12e2ac9969c754c95d350f444baf099c11e7a15a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;\\lambda&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a multiset of positive integers. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a193146e791b5f63e007a243ca1b56d6dc08fe0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_n=\\{a\\in A: a\\leq n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" />. Assume that for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a64508262bb2272e129bd59c31142b17e78b6ad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />, the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1eccfbd65334353f671fb71c27b9b9f2c689b0bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> contains at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/e/c0e64b7126f2100c61306fcac34e3020b564444e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\lambda$\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> numbers. Show that there are infinitely many <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a64508262bb2272e129bd59c31142b17e78b6ad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> for which the sum of the elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1eccfbd65334353f671fb71c27b9b9f2c689b0bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> is at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/e/38ed64d195bacb59a2ee995012e9f56f5f260242.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\\lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" />. (A multiset is a set-like collection of elements in which order is ignored, but repetition of elements is allowed and multiplicity of elements is significant. For example, multisets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/62511f4d99c1621775385afa593225a56e41f220.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/c/23c36089517f51f966031093d606a6787e44d4a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2, 1, 3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> are equivalent, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/7/d3711c073dfc337979caa9c692c1fb81d66ac874.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 1, 2, 3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/62511f4d99c1621775385afa593225a56e41f220.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> differ.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO\" title=\"2015 USAMO\">2015 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2015\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2014 USAMO Problems\">2014 USAMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2016 USAMO Problems\">2016 USAMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018060902\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.066 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 336/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1273/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 82/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10789/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.094      1 -total\n 56.57%    6.842      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 40.67%    4.919      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_